    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "b52337f546b9e5953cf1963383376f08",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><div class=\"admonition warn\">\n<span class=\"admonition-title\">One real gotcha, worth knowing before you hit it</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Some of these models are <strong>reasoning</strong> models \u2014 <code>gpt-oss-120b</code> is one. They spend tokens thinking before they answer, and that thinking comes back in a separate <code>reasoning</code> field rather than in <code>content</code>. If you set <code>max_tokens</code> too low, the budget is consumed by reasoning and <strong><code>content</code> comes back empty with <code>finish_reason: \"length\"</code></strong> \u2014 not an error, just nothing.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Two ways to not get bitten: give reasoning models room (600+ tokens), or pick a non-reasoning model when you want a direct answer. The dropdown above is ordered non-reasoning-first for exactly this reason.</span>\n</div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "5ad257cfdfe4b0cfb106ab0f058f1441",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h2 id=\"3-a-document-becomes-a-row\">3. A document becomes a row</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This is where inference stops being a chat toy. You hand it unstructured text and a schema, and you get back JSON that validates \u2014 every time, because the schema is enforced during generation rather than hoped for in the prompt.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For a document-heavy operation this is the whole game: procedures, findings, supplier submittals and inspection reports go in; queryable rows come out.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>The text below is synthetic</strong> \u2014 written for this demo. It resembles a nonconformance report but describes nothing real. Paste something of your own over it and re-run; that is a better demo than anything prepared in advance.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Run it with the default extraction instruction first, and <strong>watch the <code>disposition</code> field</strong>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "cecd7ff53f1a336f1c675cd88bbd7d76",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><marimo-ui-element object-id='nWHF-0' random-id='e0d73109-ceba-9a19-2a5e-0ce1bfc7af33'><marimo-text-area data-initial-value='&quot;NONCONFORMANCE REPORT NCR-2026-0412&#92;nLine 3, Final Assembly. Raised 2026-08-19 by K. Osei (Quality Inspector II).&#92;n&#92;nDuring receipt inspection of safety-critical valve assemblies (PO 4500-11872,&#92;nsupplier Halstead Flow Systems), 3 of 12 assemblies were found with material&#92;ncertifications that do not match the heat numbers stamped on the bodies.&#92;nAffected tags: V-1104A, V-1104C, V-1106B.&#92;n&#92;nApplicable requirements: ISO 9001:2015 Clause 8.7; AS9100D Clause 8.7.1.&#92;nProcedure QA-PROC-208 Rev 5 governs disposition.&#92;n&#92;nDisposition: USE-AS-IS rejected. Recommended REWORK pending supplier re-certification.&#92;nSupplier notified 2026-08-20. Engineering evaluation ER-2026-0155 opened.&#92;nSafety significance: none identified pending evaluation. Status: OPEN.&#92;nTarget closure 2026-09-30.&quot;' data-label='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eSource document&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;' data-placeholder='&quot;&quot;' data-disabled='false' data-debounce='true' data-full-width='true' data-rows='14'></marimo-text-area></marimo-ui-element><marimo-ui-element object-id='nWHF-1' random-id='ae18498f-2078-81f6-42d0-38448f46d813'><marimo-radio data-initial-value='&quot;As written (the obvious instruction)&quot;' data-label='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eExtraction instruction&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;' data-options='[&quot;As written (the obvious instruction)&quot;,&quot;Negation-aware (after evaluating)&quot;]' data-inline='false' data-disabled='false'></marimo-radio></marimo-ui-element><marimo-ui-element object-id='nWHF-2' random-id='bcea12bf-5c30-ac3c-008f-6b8ca67db51f'><marimo-button data-initial-value='0' data-label='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eExtract to JSON&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;' data-kind='&quot;neutral&quot;' data-disabled='false' data-full-width='false'></marimo-button></marimo-ui-element></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
