          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h2 id=\"take-this-with-you\">Take this with you</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook is a single Python file with its dependencies declared inline. To run it anywhere:</span>\n<div class=\"language-sh codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nb\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">WANDB_API_KEY</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"&lt;your key from wandb.ai/authorize&gt;\"</span>\nuvx<span class=\"w\"> </span>marimo<span class=\"w\"> </span>edit<span class=\"w\"> </span>--sandbox<span class=\"w\"> </span>cw_inference_first_run.py\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>--sandbox</code> reads the dependency list from the top of this file and builds its own environment, so there is nothing to install and nothing to conflict with what you already have. (<code>uv run cw_inference_first_run.py</code> also works, but runs it headlessly as a plain script rather than opening the notebook.)</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Keys</strong> \u2014 <a href=\"https://wandb.ai/authorize\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">wandb.ai/authorize</a></li>\n<li><strong>Model catalog and pricing</strong> \u2014 <a href=\"https://wandb.ai/site/pricing/inference\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">wandb.ai/site/pricing/inference</a></li>\n<li><strong>API reference</strong> \u2014 OpenAI-compatible; anything the OpenAI Python client does, this endpoint does</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Known limit, so you hear it from us first:</strong> Serverless Inference is <strong>text-to-text only</strong> today. If part of your workload is images, scanned drawings or PDFs-as-images, that part does not run here yet \u2014 tell us and we will scope it properly rather than let you discover it in week three.</span></span>"
          }
        }
